# Particle IDs conform to the 2017 revision of the
# Particle Data Group Monte Carlo Particle Numbering Scheme
# (see http://pdg.lbl.gov/2018/reviews/rpp2018-rev-monte-carlo-numbering.pdf)
#
# B(F) = 0 due to isopin
# Experimental B(GT+) distribution from:
# M. Scott et al. (2014), https://journals.aps.org/prc/pdf/10.1103/PhysRevC.90.025801
# 
# Numerical values were digitized from the data
# in Scott et al., Fig. 3a,  because the complete distribution is not
# tabulated numerically 
# (https://web.eecs.utk.edu/~dcostine/personal/PowerDeviceLib/DigiTest/index.html)
#
# For the 250-keV Scott bins below the particle-emission threshold,
# the measured strength is assigned to known 1+ levels of 56Mn
# listed in MARLEY's Mn.dat decay scheme.
#
# If multiple 1+ levels occur within one Scott bin, the measured
# bin strength is distributed equally among those levels.
#
# Scott bins for which no 1+ level is available are omitted and
# retained below as commented entries.
#
# Above the particle-emission threshold, the original Scott bin
# energies are retained and MARLEY treats the excited nucleus
# using its continuum de-excitation model.
#
# Particle IDs and final ion charge
1 1000260560 0
